// lib/text/unicode.grav — Unicode normalization: one spelling for text that
// looks the same ("é" as one code point, or as "e" and a combining accent).
//
//   Unicode.nfc("e\u{301}") == "é"          // composed: what most text and most keyboards use
//   Unicode.nfd("é")                        // decomposed: letters, then their marks
//   Unicode.nfkc("ﬁ ²")                     // compatibility too: "fi 2" (for identifiers, search)
//   Unicode.stripAccents("Crème brûlée")    // "Creme brulee"
//
// Compare, store or index user text after NFC, and usernames or search terms
// after NFKC, so different spellings of the same thing match. Pure ASCII is
// returned as it is at once.
